WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.449 --> 00:00:07.869
I'm Dr.. Jordan B. [Peterson] a pSychology professor of the University of Toronto and Canada

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.369
I'm going to tell you the story behind the self authoring Suite Website.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:19.240
A few years ago, I realized that the students in my classes had written essays on all sorts of subjects in grade school and college

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:26.229
However, they'd never been asked to write thoughtfully about themselves about their own past experiences

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.109
personalities and visions for their futures.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:31.520
Upon reflection

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.110
This lack of opportunity struck me as strange to say the least

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:40.029
Since there's nothing more important to get straight than your own personal experience.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:46.749
At the same time I was speaking with managers at various companies about how to hire more effective workers

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:53.260
They were much more interested in how to improve the performance of poorly performing people they had already hired.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:02.439
I didn't have much to tell them at the time because improving people is very difficult. Nonetheless the two problems stuck in my mind.

00:01:04.369 --> 00:01:11.919
So I started to search for psychological interventions that could be used widely and practically to clarify and improve people's lives.

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:20.349
I already knew that people lived inside the stories they told about themselves and that they used those stories to interpret everything around them.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:25.599
While considering this I came upon, Dr. James Pennebaker's research

00:01:26.540 --> 00:01:28.599
conducted at the University of Texas at Austin.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:36.909
Dr. Pennebaker tested Sigmund Freud's theory that the release of emotions related to traumatic events could be curative.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:43.750
He had his students write for three days for 15 minutes a day about the most upsetting experiences of their lives

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:47.799
while a control group wrote about ordinary daily activities.

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:56.589
Those in the former group experienced long-term improvements in their psychological and physical health after a brief dip in mood

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.760
Not so much because of the expression of pent-up feelings however

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:04.119
But because they drew more specific causal conclusions

00:02:04.909 --> 00:02:06.909
About what had happened to them in the past.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:14.560
Dr. Laura King had her subjects write about their ideals and future goals instead, but they experienced the same benefits.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:22.219
Our research team specifically tested the effects of the future authoring program part of the self authoring suite related to goal setting

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:28.490
at McGill University in Montreal Canada and Erasmus University in Rotterdam, Holland.

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:33.320
Academically struggling McGill students increased their grades by

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:39.050
25% in one year and decreased their dropout rates from 30% to zero

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:42.020
the same thing happened at Erasmus University

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.839
with more than 1,200 business students.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.499
These effects do not just apply to students either

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:57.230
Dr. Frank Schmidt, one of the world's outstanding industrial psychologists, has demonstrated that participating in such programs

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:02.060
Makes all kinds of people substantially more effective or whatever they are doing

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:11.630
People who complete such programs appear to benefit because the careful articulation of their experiences, past, present and future

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.649
decreases misery related to threat and uncertainty and

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:22.070
Increases happiness and hope which people experience when they progress towards somewhere they truly want to be

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:29.840
When complicated experiences are carefully put into words the manner in which they are represented in the brain changes

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:36.139
They move from the areas associated with stressful emotion demanding constant physical readiness

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:39.769
To the areas associated with detailed comprehension and understanding

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.880
This makes articulate people less stressed and more

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:48.169
informed about how to be successful now and in the future

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:53.600
It is for these reasons that we developed the Self Authoring Suite a set of four

00:03:53.880 --> 00:04:01.130
interactive online writing programs and are offering them to anyone who wants to concentrate on improving his or her life.

00:04:01.799 --> 00:04:03.799
If you want to understand yourself better

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:11.509
Become less anxious and happier and commit yourself more firmly to your education career or your relationships

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.090
these programs will help

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.959
a lot

00:04:15.959 --> 00:04:22.159
Each of the programs is composed of a series of interactive web pages that present you with specific personal questions

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:26.330
This simplifies and guides the difficult process of personal writing

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:31.370
Each program requires careful thought and takes several hours to complete

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:39.080
It is better to write over a number of days so that you have time to think and because sleep aids the process

00:04:40.110 --> 00:04:45.559
The writing is challenging, but the experimentally documented benefits are worth it

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:54.950
The past authoring program helps you write an autobiography. It will present you with pages like this introducing you to the program

00:04:56.700 --> 00:05:00.210
And providing psychologically sound advice and information

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:11.210
It will then ask you to start writing dividing your life into seven epochs or sections and describing the important experiences of each

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:18.200
The two present are three programs help you address your personality faults and capitalize on your virtues

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:23.690
When you start either of these programs you will also be presented with instruction pages

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:31.580
Then you'll be provided with a list of adjectives some of which will accurately define you and be asked to select six to nine

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:35.089
Describing your faults if you're feeling up to a challenge

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:38.509
Or your virtues if you could use a boost

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.609
You will then be asked to rank order these adjectives and to write a paragraph

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:49.220
describing a time when each had a specific effect on your life the future authoring program

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:52.609
Helps you define the future that would work best for you

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:59.239
Three to five Years down the road and just as importantly to describe the future you want to avoid

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:04.549
It starts with some questions like these which will start you thinking in the right direction

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:20.430
then it will ask you to write freely about what you want and don't want and about how to justify your decisions

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:22.800
and stay on the right track

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:27.119
The programs contain much more detail than this brief summary presents

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:31.530
Here are the sorts of additional questions you will be asked to consider

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.099
What were your 10 most important experiences?

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.620
Where they positive or negative?

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:41.699
How did each experience change you or your view of other people?

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:45.660
Were there things that you should have done differently?

00:06:46.600 --> 00:06:49.919
Are you the life of the party do you feel comfortable around people?

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:52.740
Do you think before you act?

00:06:53.320 --> 00:06:57.030
Are you full of ideas? Are you a sensible person?

00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.939
Do you do things according to a plan?

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:02.850
Are you too quiet around strangers?

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.000
Do daydream too much?

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:09.330
What is one thing that you could do better?

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:12.270
What do you want to learn about?

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.689
How should you handle your drinking or drug use?

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.440
Describe your ideal social life

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:27.329
You may choose to complete any or all of the four programs

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:33.779
You will be given a confidential username and account password and your writing will be securely stored

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:41.669
Once you have completed each program you'll receive an organized comprehensive email laying out the work that you have done

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:47.099
You can return to the programs in the future to edit and update your work

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:54.090
Many people do not understand who they are where they are or where they are going

00:07:54.760 --> 00:08:00.059
In consequence instead of attempting those actions that would make their lives as valuable as possible

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:02.940
things just happen to them

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:05.190
and they're often not good

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:11.820
Carefully answering all the questions in the Self Authoring Suite in your own words will clear the fog from your vision

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:14.460
make you healthier and stronger

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:21.059
and increase the chances that you will exist in a manner that justifies all the trouble that life inevitably presents

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:26.459
This will help you be a good person for yourself and for other people

00:08:27.850 --> 00:08:30.479
Carve yourself a new and better you

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:37.320
There's no sense slouching around miserably when you can aim for what you should have and get it

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:40.770
Good luck with the programs

